                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2903a42c-6087-3bdd-aadf-ec4598b4d24b",
                        "entry_id": "72e68a7e-c6fa-34a2-a11e-8744827e20af",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of, related to, or having characteristics of parody."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "43e07392-217b-4e31-aa9e-fb2cc355ffd4",
                                "sense_id": "2903a42c-6087-3bdd-aadf-ec4598b4d24b",
                                "text": "All gender is parodic in the sense that it is all imitative, but some forms are more parodic than others because that imitativeness is exposed."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3b685dc7-c70c-4a79-99df-87715836be9e",
                                "sense_id": "2903a42c-6087-3bdd-aadf-ec4598b4d24b",
                                "text": "From this common background, the G author/redactor seems to have chosen to highlight the more parodic elements in the tradition, while muting the more serious or somber representation of Aesop's heroic end."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a936bd89-ffbe-46a1-9c66-4c02d583808b",
                                "sense_id": "2903a42c-6087-3bdd-aadf-ec4598b4d24b",
                                "text": "So even the pastiche one might expect to be the most parodic, the fiercest with the \"target\" author, turns into—at worse^([sic])—an amusing exercise in self-congratulation, of Proust, by Proust."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
